/-!
# Affine blowup algebras

Let `R` be a ring and `I ⊆ R` an ideal. The *blowup algebra*, or *Rees algebra*, of the pair
`(R, I)` is the graded `R`-algebra `Bl_I(R) = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} Iⁿ = R ⊕ I ⊕ I² ⊕ ⋯`, with the summand
`Iⁿ` placed in degree `n`; Mathlib has it as `reesAlgebra I`, realized as the subalgebra
`⨁_{n ≥ 0} Iⁿ Xⁿ` of `R[X]`, where the degree `n` summand is spanned by the monomials `x Xⁿ` with
`x ∈ Iⁿ`. Let `a ∈ I` and write `a⁽¹⁾` for `a` viewed as an element of degree `1` of `Bl_I(R)`.
The *affine blowup algebra* `R[I/a]` is the degree zero part `(Bl_I(R))_{(a⁽¹⁾)}` of the
localization of `Bl_I(R)` at `a⁽¹⁾`: an element of it is represented by an expression `x/aⁿ` with
`x ∈ Iⁿ`, and two representatives `x/aⁿ` and `y/aᵐ` define the same element if and only if
`aᵏ(aᵐx - aⁿy) = 0` for some `k ≥ 0`.

This file defines `R[I/a]` in that second, concrete form, as the `R`-subalgebra of a localization
`S` of `R` away from `a` generated by the fractions `y/a` with `y ∈ I`. When `a ∈ I` the elements
of this subalgebra are exactly the fractions `x/aⁿ` with `x ∈ Iⁿ`, since `aᵐ x ∈ I^(n + m)` for
`x ∈ Iⁿ`, and `x/aⁿ = y/aᵐ` holds in `S` if and only if `aᵏ(aᵐ x - aⁿ y) = 0` for some `k`; so the
two descriptions define the same `R`-algebra, and the second involves no quotient by torsion
because a fraction with vanishing image in `S` already vanishes in `(Bl_I(R))_{(a⁽¹⁾)}`.

## Main definitions

* `affineBlowupAlgebra I a S` : the affine blowup algebra `R[I/a]`, as an `R`-subalgebra of a
  localization `S` of `R` away from `a`.
* `affineBlowupFraction I a S hy` : the fraction `y/a` of an element `y ∈ I`, one of the
  generators of `R[I/a]`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 052Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/052Q)

## Tags

blowup algebra, Rees algebra, affine blowup algebra, localization

-/

@[expose] public section

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R]

/-- The affine blowup algebra `R[I/a]` of an ideal `I` of a ring `R` and an element `a : R`,
defined as the `R`-subalgebra of a localization `S` of `R` away from `a` generated by the
fractions `y/a` with `y ∈ I`. For `a ∈ I` its elements are exactly the fractions `x/aⁿ` with
`x ∈ Iⁿ`. -/
@[stacks 052Q]
public def affineBlowupAlgebra (I : Ideal R) (a : R) (S : Type*) [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
    [IsLocalization.Away a S] : Subalgebra R S :=
  Algebra.adjoin R {z : S | ∃ y ∈ I, z = IsLocalization.mk' S y ⟨a, Submonoid.mem_powers a⟩}

/-- The fraction `y/a` in the affine blowup algebra `R[I/a]`, for `y ∈ I`, one of the generators
of the subalgebra. -/
public noncomputable def affineBlowupFraction (I : Ideal R) (a : R) (S : Type*) [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] [IsLocalization.Away a S] {y : R} (hy : y ∈ I) : affineBlowupAlgebra I a S :=
  ⟨IsLocalization.mk' S y ⟨a, Submonoid.mem_powers a⟩, Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩⟩

/-- For `y ∈ I`, `a · (y/a) = y` in `R[I/a]`. -/
public theorem algebraMap_mul_affineBlowupFraction (I : Ideal R) (a : R) (S : Type*)
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [IsLocalization.Away a S] {y : R} (hy : y ∈ I) :
    algebraMap R (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S) a * affineBlowupFraction I a S hy =
      algebraMap R (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S) y :=
  Subtype.ext <| (mul_comm _ _).trans <| IsLocalization.mk'_spec S y ⟨a, Submonoid.mem_powers a⟩
